# 🐳 Containerized Flask Application on AWS

A hands-on cloud engineering project that demonstrates how to containerize a Python Flask REST API using Docker and deploy it on AWS using Amazon ECR and Amazon ECS. The project also explores automated deployment to an EC2 instance using GitHub Actions and SSH.

## 🎯 Project Objective

To develop a basic Flask application, package it into a Docker container, and understand the workflow for building, testing, storing, and deploying containerized applications on AWS.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Application programming |
| Flask | REST API development |
| Gunicorn | Production WSGI server |
| Docker | Containerizing the application |
| Amazon ECR | Storing Docker images |
| Amazon ECS | Running and managing containers |
| Amazon EC2 | Virtual machine hosting and deployment experiments |
| GitHub | Source code management |
| GitHub Actions | Automating deployment workflows |
| SSH | Secure remote deployment |
| Linux Shell Script | Deployment automation |

## 🏗️ Architecture

```text
             Developer
